{"text": "KINGSPORT TIKES NEWS\n\nkrNosPoRT, TH\noarLy 4,547\n\nOpinion\n\nTHURSDAY\n\nJAN 7 1993\n\nEuirontal,\n\nEPA officials are\n\nThe EnVirosmental Protection\nAgency today will foster yet anoth-\ner hoax on the American people as\nit begins a campaign of public mis-\ninformation on the hazards of see\nondhand smoke. 7\nThe EPA will report \u00abith great\nfanfare today that \u201cpatdue\u00ae to:\nbacco smoke is a class A carcino-\ngen that kills 3,000 people\nannually, causes 150,000 to 300,000\ncases of bronchitis and pneumonia\nevery year in young children aged\nup to 18 months, worsens astama\nsymptoms for 200,000 to 1 million\nchildren yearly, and increases the\nchances that children who don't\nhave asthma will get it.\nThe report will certainly in-\ncrease efforts to eliminate smok-\ning in publie places and in the\nworkplace \u2014 especially in io-\ncations like schools where children\nface exposure. It will give lawyers\naccess to a gold mine of liability\ncases in lawsuits against compa-\nnies and individuals \u2014 even paren-\nts \u2014 that allow smoking in the\nworkplace, in public establish-\nments like taverns, perhaps even\nin the home.\nDeparting. EPA Administrator\nWiliam Reilly seems to relish the\nthought: \u201cIf you were running a\nbar or an airline or a body shop or\nwhatever and you saw your peopie\nsmoking or you allowed customers\nto smoke, you'd be opening your-\nself up 10 years, 15 years later to\nlawsuits. And people would be able\nto say you knew you were exposing\nus to cancer. There wasn't any\ndoubt about the issue. The govern-\nment has spoken on the question\u201d\n\u2014 just as it did om the question of\nasbestos in the workplace, which\ncost taxpayers billions of dollars in\n\nblowing smoke\n\nasbestos-removal programs.\n\u2018The Great American Asbestos\nHoax was launched in the late\n0s when the government pre-\ndicted ipdustrial exposure would\nlead t9775,000, deaths from asbes-\ntos-refated \u2018cancer annually.\nAsbeStos was banned everywhere.\nSchools, including those in Sullivan\nCounty, spent millions of dollars\nremoving it. And last year, the 5th\nCircuit Court of Appesis threw out\nthe ban when the EPA failed to\nmake a case even for 13 to 15\nasbestos-related cancer deaths a\nyear among heavily exposed brake\nworkers.\nThe asbestos hoax resulted\nfrom bad science and \u201cestimates\u201d\nput out by EPA that were never\nSubmitted to scientitic peer re-\nview. Suclyis the case with EPA\u2019s\nlatest cancer scare: The report to\nbe released today, according'to the\nHeritdge Foundation, is not based\n\u2018on standard scientific methods, but\nmethods specifically devised by\nEPA to yield the desired result.\nEstimates of the effects of passive\nsmoking are guesses \u2014 unscientif-\nic guesses that also have not been\nsubmitted to peer review.\nWe support bans on smoking in\nschools and have spoken on the\nhazards of smoking and the need\nfor educational programs, partic:\nularly targeted on young\u2019 people.\nBut it's critical to public policy\nthat government adheres to tradi-\ntional and rigorous scientific meth-\nods whenever it make\npronouncements dealing with such\nissues as public heaith.\nIn doing so, EPA has demon-\nstrated once again that it is hot to\nbe trusted.\n\nnv\nnN\n\n0;\n\n83882.bS;", "words": [{"text": "KINGSPORT", "x0": 269, "y0": 66, "x1": 323, "y1": 76, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "TIKES", "x0": 331, "y0": 66, "x1": 359, "y1": 76, "conf": 67.0}, {"text": "NEWS", "x0": 366, "y0": 67, "x1": 390, "y1": 76, "conf": 32.0}, {"text": "krNosPoRT,", "x0": 293, "y0": 93, "x1": 351, "y1": 101, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "TH", "x0": 360, "y0": 93, "x1": 371, "y1": 101, "conf": 82.0}, {"text": "oarLy", "x0": 281, "y0": 105, "x1": 310, "y1": 113, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "4,547", "x0": 348, "y0": 105, "x1": 383, "y1": 114, "conf": 35.0}, {"text": "Opinion", "x0": 215, "y0": 145, "x1": 399, "y1": 186, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "THURSDAY", "x0": 517, "y0": 67, "x1": 5